 r←{name}∆ListOfCountries dummy;i
⍝ If the left argument is not specified this returns a list with country names
⍝ If the left argument is specified than an integer is returned. This is the
⍝ index of that country in the list. If it is not found and error is thrown.
 r←''
 r,←⊂'France'
 r,←⊂'Germany'
 r,←⊂'Ireland'
 r,←⊂'Italy'
 r,←⊂'United Kingdom'
 :If 2=⎕NC'name'
     i←r⍳⊂name
     :If (⍴r)=i
         'Unknown country'⎕SIGNAL 6
     :Else
         r←i=⍳⍴r
     :EndIf
 :EndIf
